  "simulation_id": "uk_post_office_horizon_5actor",
  "title": "Horizon Scandal Justice Debate",
  "objective": "Explore accountability and reparations for victims of the Post Office Horizon IT scandal through stakeholder negotiations.",
  "brief": "UK Post Office Horizon IT scandal (2000-2024). Fujitsu's accounting software had bugs that made it appear sub-postmasters were stealing money. The Post Office prosecuted 700+ people, some were imprisoned, some committed suicide. It took 24 years for justice. Stakeholders: a sub-postmaster who was imprisoned for 15 months for 'theft' caused by system errors and lost their home, a Fujitsu developer aware of unresolved software bugs who was told not to disclose them in court, a Post Office internal auditor who saw patterns suggesting systemic software issues but was pressured to treat each case as individual fraud, and a local community member who lost their village post office and now travels 8 miles for basic services.",
